m in numbers:\n        product *= num\n    return product\n\nThat's it. No helper functions, linear code. That should meet all the requirements.\n</think>\n\nThe function `multiply_list` computes the product of all integers in the input list, handling edge cases like empty lists (returns 1) and zeros (returns 0). It adheres to the rules of being a single function with linear logic.\n\n<file>experiments/solution.py</file>\n```python\ndef multiply_list(numbers):\n    product = 1\n    for num in numbers:\n        product *= num\n    return product\n```"
